+<div style="padding:14px 16px;font-size:14px;"><p>For the two-device allocation problem, assess candidate $(u,v)=(2.4,0.6)$. Compute its cost and check feasibility. Consider transfers $(u,v)=(2.4-t,0.6+t)$ that preserve total flow. Find the best permitted transfer near this candidate and explain why a nonzero objective gradient does not disqualify the constrained optimum.</p>
